      "comments": 17,
      "author": "hugoarnal",
      "published": "2026-08-08T13:48:36Z",
      "bullets": [
        "Core software architectural talks highlight reducing accidental complexity, emphasizing Rich Hickey's principles of separating state, identity, and value.",
        "Key systems engineering presentations focus on distributed consensus, formal verification using TLA+, and designing fault-tolerant concurrent systems.",
        "Essential technical talks cover legacy codebase refactoring, system performance profiling, and low-level debugging techniques."
      ]
    },
    {
