      "score": 12,
      "comments": 6,
      "author": "BD103",
      "published": "2026-08-08T18:22:36Z",
      "bullets": [
        "Modern OpenSSH private keys use the openssh-key-v1 format, replacing legacy OpenSSL PEM wrappers with length-prefixed binary structures.",
        "Encrypted private keys protect payloads using ciphers like AES-256-CTR and key derivation via bcrypt_pbkdf with configurable rounds and salts.",
        "Key files explicitly serialize public components, key types like ssh-ed25519, and check integers to validate correct decryption passphrase attempts."
      ]
    },
